title: 'Probe p10m-repo-context: how to load repo context while repo hooks stay off'
summary: Real claude 2.1.303 under the generated session profile, pass. disableAllHooks in --settings also kills the kernel's own --settings hooks. --add-dir skills are not loaded while the project source is off. A --plugin-dir loads skills/agents/commands (namespaced project:x), and an UNSTRIPPED plugin skill's frontmatter hooks fire (PreToolUse, Stop). --add-dir <repo> plus CLAUDE_CODE_ADDITIONAL_DIRECTORIES_CLAUDE_MD=1 loads CLAUDE.md with @imports under --setting-sources user, without the add-dir's skills or hooks. A scratch CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR has no login (keychain credentials are keyed by the config dir), so the model arms need the real user layer.
